# This directory *is* the disposable $HOME (see .envrc), so a session writes
# its own state here. Name what a session is known to write, and nothing
# more: anything unnamed lands in `git status` as an untracked file, which is
# how this room finds out that something new pollutes it.
#
# Adding a line is therefore a discovery, not housekeeping -- say what wrote
# it. Clearing the room is `git clean -xd home/`, and the -x is needed
# precisely because these paths are ignored.

# Re-include everything first: the user's ~/.config/git/ignore hides
# `**/.claude/settings.local.json`, `**/CLAUDE.local.md`, `tmp/`, and `*.log`
# in every repo, and each of those is something this room needs to see. What
# the room reports must not depend on a file outside the repo.
!/**

# Claude Code's config dir, per .envrc
/.config/claude/.claude.json
/.config/claude/.credentials.json
/.config/claude/.last-cleanup
/.config/claude/backups/
/.config/claude/projects/
/.config/claude/sessions/
